WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.576 --> 00:00:04.037
- I'm expecting an accurate
representation of our country.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.913
- I'm not.

00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:08.500
- I'm expecting to get a
lot of stereotypical ideas

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.710
of what Australian food is.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.462
- I just keep hearing
about Blooming Onions.

00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:17.462
("Flame and Smoke")

00:00:17.509 --> 00:00:19.928
- [Voiceover] Steak.

00:00:19.928 --> 00:00:22.347
- This is what we're going to
judge Outback Steakhouse on.

00:00:22.347 --> 00:00:23.724
- It smells delicious.

00:00:23.724 --> 00:00:26.852
- I actually just bent
the fork trying to cut it.

00:00:26.852 --> 00:00:28.020
(laughing)

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.647
- This is a normal fork,
and this is Kelly's.

00:00:29.647 --> 00:00:32.683
- And this is trying
Outback Steakhouse steak.

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:35.699
(steak hitting plate)

00:00:35.714 --> 00:00:36.486
- This is good steak.

00:00:36.624 --> 00:00:37.738
- This is not a good steak.

00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:39.219
- It's so dry.

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:40.574
(knife crashing on plate)

00:00:43.619 --> 00:00:44.780
- Stick to what you're good at.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.743
- You ruined my day, America.

00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:50.705
- Well, it smells like barbeque sauce.

00:00:50.751 --> 00:00:52.750
- It's American barbeque sauce.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.061
I can tell the difference.

00:00:54.061 --> 00:00:55.782
- It's literally just chicken
with barbeque sauce on it.

00:00:56.381 --> 00:00:59.217
- It's good but it's like not Australian.

00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:00.611
- I'm just going to, I'm sorry.

00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:01.058
(laughing)

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:04.598
- What's a good Australian sauce?

00:01:04.598 --> 00:01:05.849
- A bit of tomato sauce.

00:01:05.849 --> 00:01:07.366
- Tomato, not ketchup. Tomato.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.815
- This is what we call
a prawn in Australia.

00:01:13.815 --> 00:01:16.109
- Not a shrimp, it's a bloody prawn.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.486
- It's a bloody prawn.

00:01:17.486 --> 00:01:18.361
- Mmmmph

00:01:18.361 --> 00:01:19.604
- What does it taste like a macaroon?

00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:20.781
I'm sorry.

00:01:20.781 --> 00:01:22.255
- Why is everything in
this country so sweet?

00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:22.897
- Sweet.

00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:25.452
- Everything we bite
into, we taste America.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:28.955
- That was way too much
batter, but it was pretty good.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.165
- That's a definite thumbs down.

00:01:30.165 --> 00:01:31.166
- You've ruined the prawn.

00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:32.334
- We would just do straight shimp.

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:33.335
We wouldn't have anything,

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:35.462
you'd maybe have like a little
bit of bread with butter.

00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:41.066
- To the side, ok.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:42.761
- Ribs aren't really a
big thing in Australia.

00:01:42.761 --> 00:01:44.471
- No, they're definitely not.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.598
- I'm starting to feel like
this Outback Steakhouse is like

00:01:46.598 --> 00:01:47.413
- American Steakhouse.

00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:48.034
- a Texas.

00:01:48.373 --> 00:01:49.800
- Smells good. Smells like meat.

00:01:49.893 --> 00:01:51.078
- Oh, I want to live in it.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.939
- It's probably my favorite thing so far,

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:55.315
but it's not Australian.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.650
- I'm probably going to
be crucified by saying

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.151
that this is actually really good.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.237
- Like you don't really
get rib that often,

00:02:00.237 --> 00:02:01.632
so this is like a treat.

00:02:01.632 --> 00:02:02.554
- It's so good.

00:02:06.278 --> 00:02:07.452
- What's this?

00:02:07.452 --> 00:02:07.953
(laughing)

00:02:07.953 --> 00:02:10.038
- That's a Bloomin' Onion.

00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:11.623
- Is that hold on, hold on, wait.

00:02:11.623 --> 00:02:12.290
- That's one onion?

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.667
- Oh, ick.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.858
- Deep fried heaven.

00:02:14.858 --> 00:02:17.879
- Oh, I've never seen any.
I can't even eat this.

00:02:17.879 --> 00:02:18.714
- It's deep-fried onion.

00:02:18.714 --> 00:02:18.923
(laughing)

00:02:18.923 --> 00:02:20.924
- It looks like it's from Alien.

00:02:20.924 --> 00:02:21.842
- Blaaah.

00:02:23.765 --> 00:02:25.262
- It's blooming ridiculous.

00:02:25.262 --> 00:02:26.721
- Get it out of your mouth while you can.

00:02:26.721 --> 00:02:27.765
- It's actually pretty good.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.933
- I kind of don't mind it in a weird way.

00:02:29.933 --> 00:02:31.351
- I feel like if I had any more of that

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.562
I would regret it to the day I die.

00:02:33.562 --> 00:02:35.647
- I can't stand it.

00:02:35.647 --> 00:02:36.898
- All week people have been saying,

00:02:36.898 --> 00:02:40.026
"You've got to have a blooming,
Bloomin' Onion or whatever

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.070
and you're going to love it,
you're going to love it."

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.405
How wrong they were.

00:02:43.405 --> 00:02:45.824
- I'm really sad we're so
misrepresented right now.

00:02:45.824 --> 00:02:48.618
- If you want to claim us for
this, we're happy with that.

00:02:48.618 --> 00:02:51.079
- I didn't expect it to taste Australian,

00:02:51.079 --> 00:02:53.707
but I expected it to taste ok.

00:02:53.707 --> 00:02:55.709
- They've got all this American product

00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:59.045
and they've just slapped a big
fake Australian kind of like

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.798
you're going to be
Australian now restaurant.

00:03:01.798 --> 00:03:04.634
- I would like to know
who created the menu.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.715
(didgeridoo music)

00:03:10.515 --> 00:03:11.933
- The founders of Outback Steakhouse

00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:14.175
have never been to Australia.

00:03:15.145 --> 00:03:17.063
- It's a lie.

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.648
- Yeah (mumble).

00:03:18.648 --> 00:03:22.068
- Didn't want to nip over
for a bit of research there?

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.862
- That makes sense now.

00:03:23.862 --> 00:03:24.863
I mean it's ridiculous.

00:03:24.863 --> 00:03:26.656
- That's like me opening
a Turkish restaurant.

00:03:27.949 --> 00:03:28.967
- I know, that's what I'm
saying, of course we do.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.911
- From everyone in Australia to the people

00:03:30.911 --> 00:03:32.662
at Outback Steakhouse,
with all due respect

00:03:32.662 --> 00:03:36.207
- Just jump on a plane.

00:03:36.207 --> 00:03:37.417
- It's only 13 hours away?

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:40.194
- Ok just stop serving that onion thing.

00:03:43.173 --> 00:03:44.540
- [Voiceover'] What's the slogan for

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.369
Outback Steakhouse again?

00:03:46.369 --> 00:03:47.969
- [Phone message] Good day, mate.

00:03:47.969 --> 00:03:49.679
Thanks for calling Outback
Steakhouse in Glendale.

00:03:49.679 --> 00:03:52.432
We're located at 146 South
Brand Boulevard, press one.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.058
- I think he's actually Australian.

